# Project Rules

## Purpose
This file contains durable project-specific engineering rules that specialize the pinned EREI Engineering Framework without weakening its Constitution.

## Allowed Technology / Dependency Rules
Record project-specific language, framework, dependency, build, or runtime constraints.

## Coding / Structure Rules
Record conventions that materially affect maintainability, architecture, or integration.

## Data Rules
Record project-specific write, overwrite, evidence, migration, import/export, or source-of-truth constraints.

## Security Rules
Record project-specific authorization, tenant, identity, secrets, integration, or audit constraints.

## Release Rules
Record environment, deployment, QA, rollback, versioning, or Stable immutability rules.

## Operational Rules
Record observability, incident, recovery, quota, manual-step, or support constraints.

## Temporary Rules
Temporary constraints must include an owner/reason and removal condition so they do not silently become permanent architecture.

## Conflict Rule
If a project rule conflicts with the pinned Framework Constitution, surface the conflict and require an explicit architecture decision. Do not silently choose the weaker rule.
